				"max(5, round(a * 24)) + (5 - (max(5, round(a * 24)) % 17)) % 17",
				"Shot 1: Rainy day, wide aerial shot. The camera rapidly glides upward and to the left, with the ground sliding out of frame toward the bottom right. Character A bursts into view from the lower right, speeding across the screen and exiting the top right in 0.2 seconds, accompanied by a sonic boom and a trailing gust of wind.\n\nShot 2: Low-angle upward shot with Dutch angle, revealing ground at the bottom right. Character A charges rapidly from the distant horizon toward the foreground right, closing in within 0.2 seconds. He performs a low-center-of-gravity clockwise 180-degree spinning slash (a swirling air blade), with the scene slowed down for 0.5 seconds. Immediately afterward, a massive tornado erupts along the left horizon—four martial monks are lifted and flung by the storm, with heavy motion blur and speed lines throughout. Character A follows up with another clockwise 180-degree spin slash. The camera swiftly pulls back slightly, maintaining a slight low-angle perspective. Character B crouches on a rock in the upper-right foreground, facing away from the camera, left hand guarding his chest, right hand gripping his sword ready to draw, leaning forward against the storm. Character A suddenly surges from the left-side storm, lunging toward B. During the charge, he spins 720 degrees counterclockwise in place while slashing with his katana, generating swirling air currents around him. The camera instantly cuts to a 0.1-second close-up of A’s face—eyes sharp and intense—as a white energy blade streaks past, causing the camera to shake. The shot tightly follows the trajectory of the blade, seamlessly linking both strikes.\n\nThe camera immediately circles behind A, shooting from a low-angle upward view of his back. A is positioned in the left foreground, B in the center-right midground. A's katana strikes toward B, who draws his sword to parry—the blades lock. Cut to a close-up of B’s face: brow slightly furrowed, expression calm and composed, wind whipping his clothes and hair upward, filled with speed lines.\n\nThe camera pulls back again, circling around as it shoots from a low-angle upward view of A’s back, now facing away from the lens. A lowers his body, left hand bracing on the ground, right hand sweeping horizontally with his katana. A powerful white gale sweeps to the right, encircling A with turbulent airflow. B is blown skyward by the blast. A immediately leaps high into the air, striking—triggering frame extraction, negative film effect, and screen shake upon impact.  \n\nShot 3: 90-degree vertical downward tracking shot following B mid-air. B tumbles head-over-heels, hurtling rapidly to the right, with heavy motion blur. B quickly stabilizes himself. The camera orbits and zooms in on his face. As B ascends, the ground rapidly scrolls downward. B closes his eyes, focusing inward—left hand holds his sword vertically at eye level, right hand forms a seal. When he opens his eyes, golden flames erupt from his pupils. He then swings a 2D golden sword beam sharply to the left.\n\nThe camera follows the blade around to B’s back. B is in the right foreground, A in the left midground, airborne. The camera continues to pull back rapidly, with dynamic blur intensifying. A is struck by the golden beam, triggering frame extraction, negative film, and screen shake—knocking him flying 50 meters backward. An FPV camera closely follows A’s fall, capturing his slide after landing—half-kneeling, skidding 10 meters, katana planted firmly in the ground. A remains in the left foreground, back turned; B is in the far right background, with tall grass serving as a foreground obstruction. A sudden gust of wind sweeps through the grass.\n\nThen, A charges forward in 0.2 seconds, rushing toward B, creating a pressure wave that crushes the wild grass, accompanied by a sonic boom.\n\nShot 4: A charges directly from the left background toward the camera. The shot simultaneously cuts to a close-up of B’s face. A spins 720 degrees clockwise, slashing with his blade—a white 2D energy blade with black outlines sweeping past the camera. The camera rotates clockwise along the blade’s path, circling behind A for an upward shot. A stands in the lower-left foreground, back to the camera; B is in the upper-right midground, holding his sword horizontally in defense. The clash produces a violent explosion of air pressure. This connects seamlessly to Shot 2, with 0.1-second frame extraction, negative film, and screen shake effects—all rendered with extreme motion blur.\n\nShot 54: A presses down hard on the blade with both hands, lowering his body and staring intently at B. B lowers his center of gravity, gripping his sword firmly in resistance, turning his head to face A. A lifts his leg and delivers a powerful kick to B’s abdomen. The camera rapidly zooms in for a close-up—impact triggers screen shake, negative film, and frame extraction. An FPV camera circles behind B, tracking his踉跄 retreat, with maximum dynamic blur applied. B crouches down, left hand braced on the ground to stabilize himself, positioned in the right foreground, back to the camera. In the far left background, A charges forward amid a fierce gale. The camera first zooms in on A’s ferocious face, then rapidly pulls back to reveal B’s ground-level position behind, shot from an extreme low angle with exaggerated perspective. In the mid-left frame, B raises both hands, wielding a blade that extends diagonally from the upper-right corner of the screen straight toward the lens, accompanied by a white 2D light trail. B immediately leans backward and sidesteps, narrowly avoiding the strike as the blade whips past. The evasive motion is slowed down—raindrops freeze midair into suspended droplets—before B rolls backward and lands in a half-crouch.  \n\nCut to Shot 6: B’s silhouette in a half-crouch occupies the foreground left; A remains distant in the deep background. B lunges forward with his sword, the camera closely following with intense motion blur. With his left foot, he delivers a swift kick toward A, while the sword in his right hand gathers golden energy. The camera zooms in on the kicking leg, and upon impact with A’s right arm, the frame triggers frame extraction, negative film effect, and violent shaking. Pulling back to a low-angle medium shot, tall grass obscures the foreground. On the right, B’s back is visible, while A stands on the left. B retracts his leg and performs a 180-degree counterclockwise spinning slash—the golden sword aura strikes A’s blade, knocking him back ten meters.  \n\nThe shot cuts to B’s right hand gripping the sword. After drawing two circular arcs with the blade, he reverses his grip and thrusts it into the ground. The camera then zooms in on his face, where golden backlighting rises from below, enveloping his entire body. B closes his eyes and forms a seal, uttering: “My Vow—Hell Shall Not Be Empty.” As he opens his eyes, golden light erupts from his pupils. The camera sharply zooms into his eye, accompanied by intense motion blur. Torrential rain pelts his body, and the wind flails his long hair.  \n\nShot 7: A low Dutch angle side view captures A’s profile, with grass blocking the left foreground. A raises his hand, slashing across the frame, gasping and cursing furiously as rain and wind batter his face. He swiftly swings his blade from the upper-right distance toward the lower-left foreground, the edge slicing directly toward the lens, releasing a burst of white airflow. Instantly, A rockets out of frame, leaving behind a sonic boom and a swirling vortex.  \n\nShot 8: Wide远景 (long shot) with a Dutch angle, grass concealing A’s lower half. A occupies only 8% of the frame. In 0.2 seconds, he surges leftward at high speed toward B, the wind pressure flattening wild grass and leaving a shockwave trail. He pierces through B’s body and exits violently from the right. B, occupying 8% of the frame, remains in a half-crouch, supporting his sword and forming a seal. 0.8 seconds later, a colossal tornado erupts beneath B, filling 40% of the screen, its force crushing the surrounding grass.  \n\nShot 9: An extremely low-angle upward shot reveals A’s bloodied side face, drenched by rain, his hair whipped sideways by the wind. A struggles for breath. The camera jerks sharply to the left, focusing on the tornado a hundred meters away. Wind pressure impacts the lens, and golden light pulses from within the storm. The image vibrates intensely (B remains off-screen throughout). The tornado disintegrates in a golden explosion. The camera swiftly lifts skyward, the entire sky turning gold, as radiant golden swords cascade downward. The camera retreats behind A, blades streaking past the lens, then ascends high before diving down to approach A’s face. Golden light surrounds him, his pupils contract violently, illuminated entirely by the glow. The final frame flashes white."
